{
 "version": "Antigravity CLI 1.5.3 (agy), macOS 27.0.1 (26A434) arm64, signed in, in a plain PTY outside herdr and herdr-core (2026-11-07)",
 "method": "No core ran. after-first-prompt is HostProcessReader's own macOS open-file read (lsof -nP -a -d 0-65535 -Fn -p, the awk verbatim) of a probe's agy, every G row in order. at-prompt is the same process's plain `lsof -nP -c agy` two minutes before its first prompt, cut to numbered descriptors with an absolute path, which is what that read keeps. The follow-* scenes are one agy sampled once a second with `lsof -nP -a -p <pid> -F n` and the resumed-* and *-instance scenes two more sampled every 0.1 s; those samplers kept only presence/, brain/ and conversations/ paths. pid, name (`ps -o comm=`), argv where the probe started agy, and files are recorded; parent, start (the probe's own start time in lstart form, not read with ps) and HC_SCOPE are written for the tests. HOME was the account's real home. The account name became developer, and the scratch directory /Users/developer/lab. Every UUID became a synthetic one, consistent within the file and in sort order: conversations 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000101 to 0105, ~/.gemini/config/projects files 0201 to 0207, the crash log 0301.",
 "observed": "agy holds exactly one <root>/presence/<conversation id>.lock: from the first prompt of a new conversation, and from about 0.2 s after start for --conversation <existing id>. /clear and /fork move it to the new conversation at once and keep the earlier conversation's brain/<id> folder and conversations/<id>.db open. /exit releases it. A second agy opened on a conversation already open shows `Conversation already open` and holds the brain folder and database but never the lock, not even after the first exits. --conversation <unknown id> warns `conversation \"<id>\" not found` and creates no lock, folder or database. Lock files stay after their process exits (19 were on disk before the probes). The process also holds ~/.gemini/config/projects/<uuid>.json files, which name projects, not conversations.",
